    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A rhythmic stuttering pattern can be a bit more challenging to diagnose, but it's not uncommon for streetlights to exhibit unusual behavior, especially if they're exposed to the elements. I've heard of cases where a faulty transformer or a malfunctioning control unit can cause a streetlight to stutter or flicker in a specific pattern. It's possible that the issue is more complex than just a bad bulb, but it's also possible that it's a simple case of a loose connection or a worn-out component.\n\nYou know, it's a bit like trying to catch a mischievous band of goblins - you need to observe their behavior carefully and look for patterns. In this case, the rhythmic stuttering pattern might be a clue to the underlying cause of the issue. I'd recommend taking a closer look at the streetlight's wiring and control unit, and see if you can identify any potential causes. If you're not comfortable with DIY electrical work, it's always best to leave it to the professionals.",
